{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"python-snippets","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Python Snippets","description":"Functions, classes, dataclasses, context managers, comprehensions, pytest and asyncio.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Snippets"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","contributes":{"snippets":[{"language":"Python","path":"snippets/python.json"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"snippets/python.json":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"{\n  \"Main guard\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"main\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"def main() -> None:\",\n      \"\\t$0\",\n      \"\",\n      \"\",\n      \"if __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\",\n      \"\\tmain()\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"if __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\"\"\n  },\n  \"Function with types\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"def\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"def ${1:name}(${2:arg}: ${3:str}) -> ${4:None}:\",\n      \"\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"${5:Summary.}\\\"\\\"\\\"\",\n      \"\\t$0\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A typed function\"\n  },\n  \"Class\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"cls\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"class ${1:Name}:\",\n      \"\\tdef __init__(self, ${2:arg}) -> None:\",\n      \"\\t\\tself.${2:arg} = ${2:arg}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"\\t$0\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A class\"\n  },\n  \"Dataclass\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"dc\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"from dataclasses import dataclass\",\n      \"\",\n      \"\",\n      \"@dataclass\",\n      \"class ${1:Name}:\",\n      \"\\t${2:field}: ${3:str}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A dataclass\"\n  },\n  \"With open\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"wo\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"with open(${1:path}, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as ${2:f}:\",\n      \"\\t$0\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Open a file\"\n  },\n  \"Try except\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"tc\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"try:\",\n      \"\\t$1\",\n      \"except ${2:Exception} as ${3:e}:\",\n      \"\\t$0\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"try / except\"\n  },\n  \"List comprehension\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"lc\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"[${1:x} for ${1:x} in ${2:items} if ${3:True}]\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A list comprehension\"\n  },\n  \"Dict comprehension\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"dcmp\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"{${1:k}: ${2:v} for ${1:k}, ${2:v} in ${3:items}}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A dict comprehension\"\n  },\n  \"Argparse\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"arg\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"import argparse\",\n      \"\",\n      \"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\\\"${1:What it does}\\\")\",\n      \"parser.add_argument(\\\"${2:path}\\\", help=\\\"${3:help}\\\")\",\n      \"args = parser.parse_args()\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"An argparse parser\"\n  },\n  \"Pytest test\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"test\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"def test_${1:name}():\",\n      \"\\tassert $0\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A pytest test\"\n  },\n  \"Pytest fixture\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"fix\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"import pytest\",\n      \"\",\n      \"\",\n      \"@pytest.fixture\",\n      \"def ${1:name}():\",\n      \"\\treturn $0\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A pytest fixture\"\n  },\n  \"Async main\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"amain\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"import asyncio\",\n      \"\",\n      \"\",\n      \"async def main() -> None:\",\n      \"\\t$0\",\n      \"\",\n      \"\",\n      \"asyncio.run(main())\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"An asyncio entry point\"\n  },\n  \"Logging\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"log\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"import logging\",\n      \"\",\n      \"log = logging.getLogger(__name__)\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Module logger\"\n  },\n  \"Context manager\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"ctx\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"class ${1:Name}:\",\n      \"\\tdef __enter__(self):\",\n      \"\\t\\treturn self\",\n      \"\",\n      \"\\tdef __exit__(self, exc_type, exc, tb) -> None:\",\n      \"\\t\\t$0\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A context manager class\"\n  },\n  \"Pathlib read\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"pl\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"from pathlib import Path\",\n      \"\",\n      \"text = Path(${1:\\\"file.txt\\\"}).read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Read a file with pathlib\"\n  }\n}\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Python Snippets\n\nFunctions, classes, dataclasses, context managers, comprehensions, pytest and asyncio.\n\nType a prefix and press Tab. 15 snippets.\n\n| Language | Prefix | What it inserts |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Python | `main` | if __name__ == \"__main__\" |\n| Python | `def` | A typed function |\n| Python | `cls` | A class |\n| Python | `dc` | A dataclass |\n| Python | `wo` | Open a file |\n| Python | `tc` | try / except |\n| Python | `lc` | A list comprehension |\n| Python | `dcmp` | A dict comprehension |\n| Python | `arg` | An argparse parser |\n| Python | `test` | A pytest test |\n| Python | `fix` | A pytest fixture |\n| Python | `amain` | An asyncio entry point |\n| Python | `log` | Module logger |\n| Python | `ctx` | A context manager class |\n| Python | `pl` | Read a file with pathlib |\n\nThis extension runs no code and asks for no permissions.\n"}}}